NEARS-3651 AC-ANALYTICS — documented-property deviations, live-captured via
`adb logcat -s FA-SVC:V` (log.tag.FA/FA-SVC VERBOSE), emulator-5558, 2026-09-17.

Ticket's own Analytics rule table specifies:
  order_details_opened | order_id, status, module, source=orders_list/notification/running_card
  get_help_tapped       | order_id, status

Actually fired (both live-observed, matching docs/platform/analytics-events.md as
shipped — i.e. the deviation is documented, not accidental, but still not what the
ticket's AC text names):

09-17 22:41:38.755  1560 10272 V FA-SVC  : Logging event: origin=app,name=order_details_opened,params=Bundle[{module=grocery, screen=order_details, ga_event_origin(_o)=app, ga_screen_class(_sc)=MainActivity, ga_screen_id(_si)=-3371623957355893136, ga_screen(_sn)=/order-details, order_status=delivered, order_id=91131}]

  -> "status" shipped as "order_status" (renamed); "source" property is ABSENT
     entirely (spec required source=orders_list/notification/running_card).

09-17 22:42:52.407  1560 10664 V FA-SVC  : Logging event: origin=app,name=get_help_tapped,params=Bundle[{screen=order_details, source=text_link, ga_event_origin(_o)=app, ga_screen_class(_sc)=MainActivity, ga_screen_id(_si)=-3371623957355893134, ga_screen(_sn)=/order-details, order_id=91131}]

  -> "status" property is ABSENT entirely (spec required order_id, status).

Not a blocker by itself (context IS present in a different shape — screen/source were
added even where the ticket didn't ask, which is defensible as an improvement), but it
is a literal deviation from AC-ANALYTICS's "documented properties ... with the
documented values" requirement, flagged as a task_bug per the QA gate's own rule that a
brief/AC mismatch is itself a defect source.

For contrast, reorder_tapped / reorder_basket_conflict_shown / reorder_basket_choice
(OD8) fired with FULL context blocks (module, screen, section, source, order_id, plus
extras like other_store_count) — the richer shape IS achievable in this codebase, the
2 events above are simply inconsistent with it.
